{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id595050067"}, "name":{"label":"An2bR"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-07-20T01:56:59-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"4.5.2"}, "id":{"label":"14325569682"}, "title":{"label":"Great for Nuerodivergents!"}, "content":{"label":"I have had this app for three years and it truly had saved my life. I have ADHD and time blindness, so I struggle to visualize and estimate my time like normal people. With this, I am visually able to see all the time in my day, and it keeps me on track with alerts/notifications for the start and end of a task so I know when to wrap up.  \n\nYou can keep your to do list in it too, and drag and drop it into your schedule when you’re ready. My whole brain is in this. \n\nIt really helped me when I was in college. When I had assignments and didn’t know when I’d be able to fit them in my schedule. And I would get alerts that I’d have an event that I probably forgot about. \n\nThen you just check everything off. And anything you didn’t get done in the day, you can just drag and drop it into tomorrow. \n\nI’ve tried a lot of different scheduling apps, and this one has been the best so far. \n\nSuper user friendly, and they consistently update it, so it only gets better.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=1499198946&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}], "updated":{"label":"2026-10-03T16:32:35-07:00"}, "rights":{"label":"Copyright 2008 Apple Inc."}, "title":{"label":"iTunes Store: Customer Reviews"}, "icon":{"label":"http://itunes.apple.com/favicon.ico"}, "link":[
